#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""capri-voice: Capri's voice sidecar. It owns the mic, the speech models and the speaker.

The avatar connects to a unix socket ($XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/capri-voice.sock) and talks
newline-delimited JSON:

  avatar -> here                       here -> avatar
  {"op":"config", stt_model, voice, speed, flow, pace}
  {"op":"listen-start"}                {"ev":"mic-open"}  {"ev":"level","v":0..1} (5 Hz)
  {"op":"listen-stop"}                 {"ev":"mic-closed"} {"ev":"heard","text":..., "why":..., "ms":{...}}
  {"op":"listen-cancel"}               {"ev":"mic-closed"}
  {"op":"say","id":n,"text":...}       {"ev":"say-start","id","text","dur_ms","step_ms","shapes"}  {"ev":"say-end","id"}
  {"op":"say",...,"unprompted":true}   (a reply he didn't ask for: Gate)   {"ev":"say-skipped","id","why"}
  {"op":"drop","id":n}                 (that turn's sentences go; the one playing stops)
  {"op":"hush"}                        {"ev":"hushed"}
  {"op":"media-hold","mode":"pause|duck|off"}   {"op":"media-release"}
  {"op":"stats"}                       {"ev":"stats", ...}

Privacy (ADVICE-ux 4.3, hard rules): the capture stream (pw-record) exists only between
listen-start and listen-stop/cancel; mic-open/mic-closed report that process, not the intent.
Audio lives in RAM and is dropped after decoding; nothing is written to disk. Everything runs
on the CPU (whisper.cpp, Kokoro on onnxruntime's CPU provider).

Test hooks (never needed in use): CAPRI_VOICE_SOURCE / CAPRI_VOICE_SINK name PipeWire nodes
to record from / play to (default: the default ones); CAPRI_VOICE_PLAYERS limits pause to
these MPRIS players (comma list); CAPRI_VOICE_DUCK_MATCH limits ducking to streams whose
application name contains it.

Other modes: --render TEXT --out F.wav [--voice V --speed S --flow F --pace P] (a sample; never the mic),
--selftest (no audio device; with the models, the graph patch and the flow rules).
"""
import json, os, re, select, shutil, signal, socket, subprocess, sys, threading, time, zlib

import numpy as np

HOME = os.path.expanduser('~')
MODELS = os.environ.get('CAPRI_VOICE_MODELS', f'{HOME}/.local/share/capri-voice/models')
RUNTIME = os.environ.get('XDG_RUNTIME_DIR', f'/run/user/{os.getuid()}')
